Table chart_of_accounts {
  id             bigint       [pk, increment]
  parent_id      bigint       [null, note: 'Self-reference. NULL = top-level header']
  code           varchar(20)  [not null, unique, note: 'e.g. 1121, 2110, 4100, 5100']
  name           varchar(255) [not null]
  type           varchar(255) [not null, note: 'asset | liability | equity | revenue | expense — IMMUTABLE']
  normal_balance varchar(255) [not null, note: 'debit | credit — IMMUTABLE']
  is_active      boolean      [not null, default: true]
  description    text         [null]
  created_at     timestamp    [null]
  updated_at     timestamp    [null]

  Indexes {
    parent_id
    (type, code)
  }

  Note: '''
  Domain: Accounting
  Model: App\Domains\Accounting\Models\ChartOfAccount

  Single master COA shared across BOTH fiscal modes. Tax-specific accounts
  (PPN Masukan 1141, PPN Keluaran 2121) are activated dynamically by the
  transaction fiscal_mode, not by maintaining two separate charts.

  STRICT LEAF NODE RULE
    is_leaf is DERIVED (children_count === 0), never a column.
    - Leaf accounts   : the ONLY accounts postable to journal_entry_items,
                        invoices, purchase orders, or cash transactions.
    - Header accounts : aggregation only, for Balance Sheet and P&L rollups.
                        Selecting one in a transaction form must be rejected.

  IMMUTABILITY
    type and normal_balance can never change after creation — the ledger
    history depends on them. code should be treated the same way: journal
    lines point at account_id, so a renamed code would silently rewrite the
    meaning of every past entry that references it.

  PROJECTS MUST NOT CREATE ACCOUNTS
    No per-project revenue accounts (no "4111 Pendapatan Project A").
    Per-project reporting is done purely through
    journal_entry_items.project_id tagging.
  '''
}

Ref: chart_of_accounts.parent_id > chart_of_accounts.id
